        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Seth Davis, Greg Gumbel, Clark Kellogg, Doug Gottlieb, Bryant Gumbel\n- Organizations: Sports Illustrated, Campus Insiders, CBS\n- Roles: writer, host, in-studio analyst, television sportscaster, play-by-play announcer\n- Events: NCAA men's college basketball coverage, Super Bowl XXXV\n\nFacts:\n- Greg Gumbel was born on May 3, 1946, and he is an American television sportscaster.\n- In 2001, Greg Gumbel became the first African-American and Creole announcer to call play-by-play for a major sports championship in the United States when he announced Super Bowl XXXV for CBS.\n- Greg Gumbel is the older brother of news and sportscaster Bryant Gumbel.\n- Seth Davis is a former writer for Sports Illustrated magazine.\n- Seth Davis is a host on Campus Insiders.\n- Seth Davis is an in-studio analyst for CBS's NCAA men's college basketball coverage with Clark Kellogg, Doug Gottlieb, and host Greg Gumbel.",
